{
  "$comment": [
    "The contact register behind section 8. This is the machine-readable twin of the prose.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM THE PROSE: two jobs need structured data, and neither can be done",
    "against markdown. (a) notify-listed.js tells each listed organisation what we publish about them",
    "and how to be removed. (b) build.js refuses to render any address on the suppression list - so a",
    "removal request is enforced at the point of publication and cannot be quietly undone by a later",
    "refresh that re-scrapes the same public page.",
    "",
    "CONTACTS POLICY: organisational contacts only, as published by the organisation itself. Never a",
    "named individual's personal mobile or private email, even where publicly findable.",
    "",
    "FIELDS",
    "  id            stable slug; NEVER reuse or renumber - the notify ledger and suppression list key on it",
    "  name          as the organisation writes it",
    "  section       which section lists them",
    "  email/phone   organisational only; null where none was verifiable",
    "  web           their live surface, which is often Facebook rather than a website",
    "  sourceUrl     where the contact was found - every notification email states this",
    "  verifiedOn    when it was last checked",
    "  contactStatus 'verified' | 'archived-possibly-stale' | 'unverified'",
    "  notifiable    false where we have no address to write to, so the notifier skips cleanly"
  ],
